### Create product 1
POST http://localhost:8081/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Mechanical Keyboard", "description": "RGB, hot-swap switches", "price": 45.00, "stockQuantity": 10 }

### Create product 2
POST http://localhost:8081/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Wireless Mouse", "price": 20.00, "stockQuantity": 5 }

### Get product (second call comes from Redis)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products/1

### Place an order (10% discount above 100.00)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "customer@example.com",
  "items": [
    { "productId": 1, "quantity": 2 },
    { "productId": 2, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### Try to buy more than in stock -> 409
POST http://localhost:8081/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "customer@example.com", "items": [ { "productId": 2, "quantity": 99 } ] }

### Pay
PATCH http://localhost:8081/api/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "PAID" }

### Ship
PATCH http://localhost:8081/api/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "SHIPPED" }

### Invalid transition (SHIPPED -> CANCELLED) -> 409
PATCH http://localhost:8081/api/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "CANCELLED" }

### Customer orders
GET http://localhost:8081/api/orders?customerEmail=customer@example.com

### Notifications for the order (created from Kafka events)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/notifications/orders/1

### Notifications for the customer
GET http://localhost:8082/api/notifications?recipient=customer@example.com
